{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall eat old long-stored.</b> The meaning: that you will be many, and because of the abundance of grain, whoever wishes will eat old, even long-stored, more than the old. It is a nif'al form. And there is one who will take the old out of his house because of the new, for he has no place to store it there. And he interprets it thus, for the sense of <b>you shall take out</b> is to the field."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:36.788318820Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}